<% hero = scene.active_player %><% game = scene.game_session %>Scene <%= scene.position %> of <%= game.scene_budget %>, <%= scene.part_of_the_story %>, <%= hero.name %>'s turn.<% if scene.first? %> This is the opening, as the plan's opening has it: show where <%= hero.name %> is and why, who is there and who they are, and end on the trouble landing on <%= hero.name %>, so the reader knows what is at stake. Reveal nothing of what the plan hides.<% else %> Pick up where the last outcome stopped, without retelling it, and keep true what the story has shown: who holds what and who knows what, where everyone is and how much time is left. <% if (found = game.clues_found).any? %>Clues found so far: <%= found.to_sentence %>.<% else %>No clue found yet.<% end %> The heroes do only what the players chose: where the way forks, the fork goes into the choices.<% end %><% if scene.last? %> Bring the story to the moment that decides it: the roll on the choice made here ends it.<% end %>
<%= hero.name %>, <%= hero.character.identity %>: <%= hero.character.sheet %>.
<% if (companions = scene.companions).any? %>In the scene with <%= hero.name %>: <%= companions.map { it.character.portrait }.join("; ") %>.
<% end %>